# ── KEY MATERIAL. Never committed, never in .env, never read at runtime. ───────
# Anything key-shaped stays out of the repo on principle, regardless of what it
# currently controls. It is deliberately NOT in .env either, because .env is
# loaded by the app and mirrored into Netlify env — a key that no running code
# path can reach cannot be leaked by one. The patterns are broad so a future key
# file cannot miss the net by being named slightly differently.
#
# ⚠️ CORRECTED 2026-07-24. This block used to claim the cold owner EOA in .keys/
# was "the root of trust for the agent registry: whoever holds it OWNS the
# agents." THAT WAS NEVER TRUE. The cold owner 0xc85b3d9BdEb… has never owned any
# agent identity on-chain. The ERC-8004 identities are owned by the agent's Circle
# DEVELOPER-CONTROLLED SCA at 0xc54d47211997aca90ef4fcfbc742a3b511b4e621 — the
# same custodial account class that holds the agent float. Confirmed on-chain:
# ownerOf(850337) == 0xc54D47211997aCA90Ef4fCfBc742a3b511B4e621.
#
# The same false claim was removed from agent-metadata/*.json when the ownership
# model was stated plainly; this copy was missed because it lives in a comment.
# Holding .keys/cold-owner.json grants NO authority over the agent identities.
# The patterns below stay anyway — key hygiene does not depend on the key
# mattering.
.keys/
*.key
*.privkey
cold-owner*.json

# ── Incidental run output from scripts/register-identity.mjs ───────────────────
# Raw dump of this wallet's NFT holdings, written as audit evidence for the
# existence check. Not credentials — just noise that shouldn't be committed
# carelessly.
# NOTE the deliberate asymmetry: agent-metadata/REGISTERED-IDENTITY.json is NOT
# ignored. The agentId is public, persisting it is the entire point of that
# script, and committing it is a durable copy of the value whose loss caused the
# orphan-wallet excavation in the first place.
# ⚠️ BROADENED 2026-07-31 — the exact-path form ALREADY FAILED ONCE. A second dump written
# as `.nft-enumeration-dd-service.json` did not match `.nft-enumeration.json` and sat
# untracked-but-unignored, one `git add .` from being committed. That is precisely the miss
# the broad `.keys/` and `*.key` patterns above exist to prevent, so this pattern is broad
# for the same reason: a future dump must not escape by being named slightly differently.
agent-metadata/.nft-enumeration*.json
